# PDF Batch Import (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/pdf-import.md`)

## Invariants
- Box axis order drives **both** prompt wording (`pdf_box_order_vars`) and parsing (`_normalize_box`). It is per endpoint: always `llm_client.box_coord_order(config)` (`LLMConfig.box_coord_order`, blank → `PDF_IMPORT_COORD_ORDER`); never read the setting directly at a new call site. Range is auto-detected (≤ 1 fractional, ≤ 1024 → /1000, else pixels ÷ downscaled dims). Use `debug=1` before changing an endpoint's order.
- The LLM sees the `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM` copy; crops are cut from the `PDF_IMPORT_RASTER_WIDTH` PNG; boxes are stored fractional.
- `_finalize_detect` runs once after all pages: custom-prompt numbering 1..N in `(page, top-Y)` order, otherwise `_stitch_continuations` re-links `continues_prev/next` and (frameless only) gives the continuation the head box's x1/x2; when `frame_snap=1` (exam), `snap_boxes_to_frames` then overwrites x from `meta[kind]['frames']` so the per-page frame wins. JS mirror `stitchContinuations` does the same. Transient `_cp/_cn` are stripped before `plan.json`. Deterministic under parallel detection. Exam plan items carry `label` (`5` / `5a` / `23-24`) plus optional `role` / `source_*` after pass 2.
- Every path that puts LLM boxes into the plan (`iter_detect`, `iter_split_detect` incl. agent repair rounds, `/redo-page`) takes `frame_snap` and ends in `apply_frame_snap` **after** stitching; the UI sends the flag on all three (when Crop width = Auto, `frameSnapActive()`) and runs `stitchContinuations` before `applyWidthPolicy`. Adding a new detection path without this re-creates the "Re-run ignores the green frame" bug. Per-page **Re-split page** re-splits root labels as whole questions (all pages), never one page's parts alone.
- On a framed page, box x1/x2 come from `meta[kind]['frames']` via `snap_boxes_to_frames` (inset `PDF_IMPORT_FRAME_INSET_PCT`). Frames are detected at stage time (`detect_page_frame` + `consolidate_frames`; odd/even pages use same-parity medians); old tokens get them lazily via `ensure_frames`. Overlay editing only through `OQBBboxEditor` — mutate the host item then `ed.restyle(item)`.
- Optional pass 2 (`iter_split_detect` / `/split-detect`): per whole-question crop, `detect_parts` then `full_width_child_box` (children inherit the parent's x1/x2 — never let pass 2 move the left edge, it breaks uniform-width alignment). Crops for pass 2 use `pad_frac=0`; one retry on `LLMError` via `_call_with_llm_retry`. `parallel=1` is gated like pass 1 (cloud + `max_concurrency > 1`); QUE is merged before SOL fans out. `Subject.split_parts_default` seeds the wizard checkbox; the live tick auto-runs pass 2. Nested parts are plain labels (`4d` + `4di`); re-splitting `4d` only replaces `4d` and its descendants (`_replace_group`).
- **Stem fill** (`_split_one_group`, `split_question_png(fill_stem=)`): a reply with parts but no stem gets a stem for the strip above the first part — QUE only, the parent's first page only, plain-number or range parents (never a nested `4d`), strip ≥ `STEM_FILL_MIN_HEIGHT`, `pdf_layout.has_ink` true. It only adds a box. Widening a guard needs tests in `tests/test_pdf_import_plan.py`.
- **Range split** (`31-32`): pass 2 runs in range mode (`detect_parts(range_span=…)` → `PDF_PART_RANGE_*` prompts → `parse_part_boxes(range_span=…)` / `normalize_range_box_label`) and yields stem `31-32` + questions `31`, `32` (`source_label = 31-32`). Never send a range through the lettered-part path (letters are rejected, `31` normalises to `stem`). Skip when `range_has_own_questions`.
- Pass 1 retries a page once on `LLMError`; a page that still fails is `error` + `page.failed` and must render as failed (`setPageFailed`), never as "no regions". The numbering banner (`numberingIssues`: drop / gap / repeat) is how users notice a failed or missed page.
- `unlockPageJobs` restores every `.job-busy-src` in the document — busy sources (Step 2 **Detect parts**) can sit outside `#reviewBody` — and sets `disabled = false` on every `.split-actions button`, so an inert row control is styled, never `disabled`.
- Row **+ ▾** (`rowAddOptions` / `addToQuestion`) adds a stem / part / sub-part to the row's question only (new questions = Add box ▾). Turning a whole question into stem + parts stores `source_*` on **all** its boxes on every page before shrinking (Unsplit and WHOLE rely on it). A cut leaves the pair in `joinedEdges` so resizing one edge moves the other.
- Box-list rows are placed by box top inside `addBoxDom` (plan order is not reading order; split results are appended). The sticky `#jobStrip` mirrors `setStatus` / `showProgress` / `updateProgress` / `appendLog`; a new job without progress events calls `stripStart` / `stripEnd`. Arrow-key nudge and H-hides-magnifier live in `OQBBboxEditor`, not in the page.
- Every PDF-import `llm_client.chat` passes `timeout=llm_timeout()` (`PDF_IMPORT_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, 0 = endpoint's); keep that on new call sites. Exception: `/redo-page` (no retry, user waits) passes `redo_timeout(cfg)` through `detect_single_page(timeout=)`.
- **Crop width** is one select (`cropWidthSel`: `auto` frame > uniform, `uniform`, `model`; `PDF_IMPORT_WIDTH_MODE_DEFAULT`, ADR-014). Never reintroduce separate frame-snap / uniform toggles.
- **Renumbering moves whole questions** (root = number prefix or range; a split range and its child questions are one unit via `groupRootOf(it, kind)`, which also catches pass-1 boxes `27`, `28` beside a `27-28` box that have no `source_label`): `setItemRoot` rewrites label **and** `source_label`. Insert ripples +1 only while numbers clash; delete cascades only when the root's last box goes; `renumberFromPage` keeps a page-top box's number only when `continuesFrom` says it continues (persisted `cont` / `cp`·`cn` / same `source_label` root / same range / part label); a bare repeated number without `cont` is a new question. Code that creates a continuation box must set `cont: true` (stitch, Unsplit do; the row **Cont.** toggle sets it by hand). Add ▾ part trims the whole box on the first part and sets `source_*` on both. `finishDraw` reads `card._addRole` first (the editor turns add mode off before `onCreate`).
- **Page range** (`parse_page_range` / `POST /stage` `page_range`): 1-based source-PDF spec (`1-8`, `3,5,12-14`) set in Step 1 **before** Load PDF. Blank = all. Applied to source pages **before** A3 split. Same spec on QUE and SOL. Junk / no matching pages → 400.
- **`role` is derived, never trusted**: `apply_derived_roles` (→ `hierarchy.derive_roles`) runs on every plan save path (`sanitize_plan`, `_finalize_detect`, `_strip_split_flags`, agent finish); the browser mirrors it in `deriveRoles`. Do not read `role` from model output or from the posted plan.
- **AI agent** (`app/pdf_agent.py`, `/pdf-import/agent`): fixed pipeline outline → locate → segment → verify/repair, LLM answers strict JSON only, code applies fixes, unresolved items go to `attention.json`. It **replaces `plan.json`**. The worker is a daemon thread keyed by token; SSE is a spectator (15 s heartbeats, `attach=1` rejoins, client drop does not cancel). Per-page verify must only expect parts on that page (`labels_on_other_pages` / `ignore_missing`) or a multi-page question will redetect itself. Hints flow through optional params only (`expected_by_page`, `page_filter`, `expected_by_parent`, `note_by_parent`, `extra_note`) — plain runs pass none. Budget via `PDF_AGENT_MAX_LLM_CALLS`. UI: experimental Step 2 strip **Run AI agent** after Load PDF — do not auto-start on load; the normal path is Detect questions + Detect parts. Spec: `docs/modules/pdf-agent.md`, ADR-010.
- IMG Split-into-parts (`question_split.iter_detect_boxes`, SSE): stitch multi-image QUE, then PDF-import **pass 2** (`detect_parts`) **once on the stitch**. Do not send each part-crop as a page. `find_parent=1` only for a full exam-page scan.
- Plan item `depends_prev: true` survives `sanitize_plan` and becomes `Question.needs_prev_parts` at commit (parts with a parent only).
- `replace_img_assets` deletes existing IMG rows first — commit **is** overwrite; the `slot_has_img` skip is the only guard. For a **root** QUE that pass-2 split, `iter_commit` writes `WHOLE` from `whole_source_crops` (pass-1 `source_box` pages) **before** the tight stem QUE. Nested stems and range stems never get WHOLE. Dashboard/generator never read WHOLE.
- Crop = box + `PDF_IMPORT_CROP_PAD_PCT`; `trim_white` defaults from `PDF_IMPORT_TRIM_WHITE_DEFAULT` (OFF); ZIP export pads but never trims. Never white-trim a frame-snapped crop horizontally — `FrameCropper` uses `crop_page(..., trim_axis='vertical')` and optional width normalise. `shrink_sides` applies to QUE only.
- Commit uses the live Step 1 paper + Step 3 versions (persisted to meta); subject change is blocked; a plan can be imported repeatedly.
- NumPy is optional: `refine` / `segment` / deskew / `detect_page_frame` need it; detect fails fast with one SSE error, deskew warns and skips; missing NumPy yields all-`None` frames.
- Staging: `<SYSTEM_PATH>/.pdf_import/<token>/` (fallback `OUTPUT_PATH`), token `^[0-9a-f]{8,40}$`, purged after 6 h. Raster workers each open their own `fitz.Document`.
- Generic (non-exam) sessions bypass the subject check and never write the DB; exam sessions are subject-admin scoped via `_pdf_load_token_meta`.
- Default endpoint: `PDF_IMPORT_DEFAULT_LLM` → `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM` → first vision endpoint (also for `guess-paper`).
- Server-side PDF picker resolves `{root, rel_path}` through the user's `RootRegistry` (`_resolve_server_pdf`); `PDF_SOURCE_PATH` defaults to `SHARED_PATH`.

## Routes
`/admin/pdf-import` + `/stage`, `/detect` (SSE, `frame_snap`), `/split-detect` (SSE), `/agent` (SSE, `frame_snap`), `/attention`, `/redo-page`, `/plan`, `/frame` (`set_manual_frame`), `/guess-paper`, `/commit`, `/export-zip`, `/discard`, `/cancel`, `/source-list` — all subject-admin scoped.

## Gotchas
- Tunables in `core/06`: raster width/workers, LLM call timeout, coord order (default; endpoints override), deskew/method/trim defaults, crop width mode default, frame inset, frame-width normalise, pad percentages. Read via `current_app.config`. Spec: `docs/modules/pdf-import.md`.
- Prompts (`PDF_*` including `PDF_PART_*` and `PDF_AGENT_*`) and their parsers live in `app/ai_prompts.py`; keep the JSON contracts in sync. Pass-2 crops use `pad_frac=0` before `full_width_child_box`. `{{expected_note}}` must stay declared in `variables` for every prompt that uses it or `render_prompt` leaves the slot in the text.
- Agent tunables (`PDF_AGENT_*`) follow the four-place rule in `system-settings.mdc`. Outline page numbers are 1-based captions; plan `page` is 0-based — convert only inside `iter_agent`.
- Do not re-import `Subject` inside `pdf_import_stage` — it is already imported at the top of `admin.py`. A local import shadows the earlier existence check and 500s Load PDF.
